---
import MotionFigure from '../relational-motion/MotionFigure.astro';
interface Props { kind: 'cut' | 'chain' | 'payment'; }
const {kind} = Astro.props;
---
{kind === 'payment' ? <MotionFigure collection="distributed/operations" kind={kind} number={3} id={'cb-payment-title'} /> : <>{kind === 'cut' && <figure class="cb-figure" data-cut aria-labelledby="cb-cut-title">
  <figcaption id="cb-cut-title"><span>Figure 1</span> One restore point, two omitted changes</figcaption>
  <div class="cb-scene">
    <label>Restore to <select data-target aria-label="Restore target for figure 1"><option value="0">Before the mistake</option><option value="1">Through the mistake</option><option value="2">Through the payment</option></select></label>
    <p class="cb-label">Original committed history →</p>
    <ol class="cb-path"><li data-event="0"><strong>Order 103</strong><span>Agreement 29.00<br/>Stock → 10 / 0 / 4</span><b data-event-result>Retained</b></li><li data-event="1"><strong>Price mistake</strong><span>P7 catalogue<br/>20.00 → 2.20</span><b data-event-result>Omitted</b></li><li data-event="2"><strong>Payment 504</strong><span>10.00 by card<br/>Order still pending</span><b data-event-result>Omitted</b></li></ol>
    <div class="cb-split"><div class="cb-box"><p class="cb-label">Restored database</p><dl><dt>P7 catalogue</dt><dd data-price>20.00</dd><dt>Order 103</dt><dd>Pending · 29.00</dd><dt>Payment 504</dt><dd data-payment>Absent</dd><dt>Recorded due</dt><dd data-due>29.00</dd></dl><p>Stock: P3 10 · P7 0 · P9 4</p></div><div class="cb-box cb-external"><p class="cb-label">Provider · outside the restore</p><strong>Accepted 10.00</strong><code>order-103-part-payment-1</code><p>The charge stays accepted at every cut.</p></div></div>
    <p class="cb-explanation" data-cut-explanation aria-live="polite">The earlier state keeps the purchase. It omits the mistake and the valid later payment record.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="cb-caption">A model of the recovery branch, assuming the selected point is covered. Order is shown without invented commit times. The provider is hypothetical and its accepted result is an input.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>The order and its stock decrement commit before the mistaken catalogue price, which commits before payment 504. A cut before the mistake excludes both later changes. A cut through the payment retains both. The external charge is unaffected.</p></details>
</figure>}
{kind === 'chain' && <figure class="cb-figure" data-chain aria-labelledby="cb-chain-title">
  <figcaption id="cb-chain-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Which points does this chain cover?</figcaption>
  <div class="cb-scene">
    <div class="cb-options"><label>Captured history <select data-history aria-label="Captured history for figure 2"><option value="history">Revision history in all three</option><option value="points">Backup points only</option></select></label><label>Retained material <select data-material aria-label="Retained material for figure 2"><option value="all">Full + B + C</option><option value="gap">Increment B missing</option></select></label></div>
    <p class="cb-label">One full-backup path · dependency order →</p>
    <ol class="cb-path cb-chain-path"><li><strong>Full A</strong><span>Complete shop<br/>at point A</span><b>Available</b></li><li data-increment-b><strong>Increment B</strong><span>Changes A → B<br/>includes mistake</span><b data-b-state>Available</b></li><li data-increment-c><strong>Increment C</strong><span>Changes B → C<br/>includes payment</span><b data-c-state>Reachable</b></li></ol>
    <div class="cb-coverage" data-coverage><div><b>A</b><span>before mistake</span><b>B</b><span>after mistake</span><b>C</b></div><div class="cb-band" data-band>Captured interior history</div></div>
    <p class="cb-explanation" data-coverage-explanation aria-live="polite">With the complete path and captured revisions, an interior cut before the mistake can be restored.</p>
    <div class="cb-new-full"><strong>A later full D starts another path</strong><span>LATEST selects that newer full path. It does not choose A because A contains the state you want.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cb-caption">A, B, C and D are symbolic backup points, not native paths, equal durations or file sizes. The history band starts at A for clarity; a full backup with revision history can also capture retained revisions before A.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>Reaching C requires full A and increments B and C. Without B, C remains a file but this path cannot reach it. Without revision history, only backup points are supported. Captured history permits interior points within its actual bounds. A newer full D is a separate starting copy.</p></details>
</figure>}
{kind === 'payment' && <figure class="cb-figure" data-reconcile aria-labelledby="cb-payment-title">
  <figcaption id="cb-payment-title"><span>Figure 3</span> Restore the record of an accepted charge</figcaption>
  <div class="cb-scene">
    <label>Provider evidence <select data-provider aria-label="Provider evidence for figure 3"><option value="accepted">Accepted · matching order and amount</option><option value="unknown">Outcome unavailable</option><option value="mismatch">Order or amount disagrees</option></select></label>
    <p class="cb-boundary">Source writes closed · candidate isolated · external dispatch disabled</p>
    <p class="cb-identity"><code>order-103-part-payment-1</code><span>Order 103 · payment 504 · 10.00 by card</span></p>
    <div class="cb-split"><div class="cb-box"><p class="cb-label">Recovered CockroachDB</p><dl><dt>Payment rows for 504</dt><dd data-count data-live>0</dd><dt>Operation mapping</dt><dd data-mapping data-live>Absent</dd><dt>Recorded due</dt><dd data-repair-due data-live>29.00</dd></dl><p>Pending order · agreed total 29.00<br/>Stock stays 10 / 0 / 4</p></div><div class="cb-box cb-external"><p class="cb-label">Provider lookup</p><strong data-provider-result data-live>Accepted · matching 10.00</strong><p>No new charge is sent.</p></div></div>
    <p class="cb-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The restored purchase is present. Its later payment and operation mapping are absent.</p>
    <div class="cb-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 3 controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span></div><div class="cb-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cb-caption">A controlled reconciliation model using the provider contract stated in the text. Only its database changes are exercised by the native drill. An unavailable or mismatched result stops before the repair.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>Restore the earlier shop with its purchase intact.</li><li>Look up the original operation at the provider and compare its immutable meaning.</li><li>For a matching accepted result, commit payment 504 and its operation mapping together.</li><li>On a repeat, verify the mapping and payment instead of inserting again.</li><li>Check 10.00 recorded, 19.00 due, pending status and stock 10/0/4. Unknown or mismatched evidence leaves the repair unresolved.</li></ol></details>
</figure>}
</>}
<script>
import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
const cut = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cut]');
if(cut){ const select=cut.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-target]')!; const draw=()=>{const n=Number(select.value);cut.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-event]').forEach((el,i)=>{el.dataset.kept=String(i<=n);el.querySelector('[data-event-result]')!.textContent=i<=n?'Retained':'Omitted';});cut.querySelector('[data-price]')!.textContent=n?'2.20':'20.00';cut.querySelector('[data-payment]')!.textContent=n===2?'10.00 recorded':'Absent';cut.querySelector('[data-due]')!.textContent=n===2?'19.00':'29.00';cut.querySelector('[data-cut-explanation]')!.textContent=['The earlier state keeps the purchase. It omits the mistake and the valid later payment record.','The mistake is now present, but payment 504 is still outside this cut.','Payment 504 is present, together with the earlier mistake. This cut cannot separate them.'][n];};select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();}
const chain=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-chain]');
if(chain){const history=chain.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-history]')!;const material=chain.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-material]')!;const draw=()=>{const gap=material.value==='gap',points=history.value==='points';chain.querySelector('[data-b-state]')!.textContent=gap?'Missing':'Available';chain.querySelector('[data-c-state]')!.textContent=gap?'Blocked by missing B':'Reachable';chain.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-increment-b]')!.dataset.kept=String(!gap);chain.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-increment-c]')!.dataset.kept=String(!gap);chain.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-coverage]')!.dataset.points=String(points);chain.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-coverage]')!.dataset.gap=String(gap);chain.querySelector('[data-band]')!.textContent=gap?'Path ends at A':points?'● A only' : 'Captured interior history';chain.querySelector('[data-coverage-explanation]')!.textContent=gap?'C still exists, but the required B is missing. This path cannot reach B, C or an interior point after A.':points?'Only the saved points A, B and C are supported. A timestamp between A and B is not made restorable by keeping more current revisions on the source.':'With the complete path and captured revisions, an interior cut before the mistake can be restored.'; if(points&&!gap)chain.querySelector('[data-band]')!.innerHTML='<b>● A</b><b>● B</b><b>● C</b>';};history.addEventListener('change',draw);material.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();}
const repair=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-reconcile]');
if(repair){const provider=repair.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-provider]')!;const accepted=['The restored purchase is present. Its later payment and operation mapping are absent.','The provider confirms the original operation: order 103, 10.00 by card. Compare this meaning before writing.','One transaction records payment 504 and the immutable operation mapping. A failure commits neither.','A repeated repair reads the same mapping and payment. It verifies equality and returns the existing result.','Payment 504 appears once. Of the agreed 29.00, 19.00 remains due. The retained purchase is not repeated.']; const draw=(s:number)=>{const ok=provider.value==='accepted',done=ok&&s>=2;repair.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=done?'1':'0';repair.querySelector('[data-mapping]')!.textContent=done?'103 · 10.00 · card → 504':'Absent';repair.querySelector('[data-repair-due]')!.textContent=done?'19.00':'29.00';repair.querySelector('[data-provider-result]')!.textContent=provider.value==='accepted'?'Accepted · matching 10.00':provider.value==='unknown'?'Unresolved outcome':'Payload mismatch';repair.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=ok?accepted[s]:s===0?accepted[0]:provider.value==='unknown'?'The provider outcome is unavailable. Keep this operation unresolved; local absence does not authorise another charge.':'The provider meaning disagrees with the retained operation. Stop and investigate; do not rewrite its identity.';};const player=stepper(repair,{steps:()=>provider.value==='accepted'?5:2,draw});provider.addEventListener('change',()=>{player.render();});}
</script>
<style>
.cb-figure{margin:2rem 0;font: .88rem/1.55 var(--font-sans)}
.cb-figure figcaption{margin-bottom:.6rem;font:1.1rem/1.5 var(--font-serif)}
.cb-figure figcaption>span{font:.7rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;margin-right:.6rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}
.cb-scene{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt)}
.cb-scene p{font:inherit;margin:.85rem 0}.cb-scene label{display:flex;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;font-size:.8rem}.cb-scene select{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.4rem;max-width:100%}
.cb-label{font-size:.75rem!important;color:var(--color-text-secondary);letter-spacing:.04em}.cb-path{list-style:none;padding:0!important;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem;margin:1rem 0!important}.cb-path li{position:relative;padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--teal);margin:0!important;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.45rem;min-width:0}.cb-path li:not(:last-child)::after{content:'→';position:absolute;right:-1rem;top:40%;color:var(--color-text)}.cb-path li span{font-size:.8rem}.cb-path b{font-size:.74rem;color:var(--color-text)}.cb-path [data-kept=false]{border-style:dashed;border-color:var(--coral)}.cb-path [data-kept=false] b{color:var(--color-text)}
.cb-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:.8rem}.cb-box{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);min-width:0}.cb-box p:first-child{margin-top:0}.cb-box p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.cb-box dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:.35rem;margin:.5rem 0}.cb-box dt{color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.76rem}.cb-box dd{margin:0;text-align:right;font-size:.82rem}.cb-external{border-style:dashed}.cb-external code,.cb-identity code{display:block;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:.76rem}.cb-external strong{display:block}.cb-explanation{border-left:3px solid var(--teal);padding:.6rem .75rem;background:var(--color-surface);min-height:3.4em}.cb-caption{font-size:.79rem!important;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.6rem 0!important}.cb-figure details{font-size:.8rem}.cb-figure summary{cursor:pointer}.cb-options{display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.cb-coverage{margin:1.2rem 0}.cb-coverage>div:first-child{display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:.4rem;font-size:.8rem}.cb-coverage span{font-size:.67rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.cb-band{border:2px solid var(--teal);padding:.4rem;text-align:center;font-size:.75rem;white-space:pre-wrap}.cb-coverage[data-points=true] .cb-band{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-left:0;border-right:0;border-top:0;border-bottom-style:dotted;white-space:normal}.cb-coverage[data-gap=true] .cb-band{border-color:var(--coral);width:34%;min-width:7rem}.cb-new-full{border-top:1px dashed var(--color-rule-strong);padding-top:.8rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;font-size:.78rem;gap:.3rem}.cb-boundary{padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);font-size:.74rem!important}.cb-identity{margin:1rem 0}.cb-identity span{display:block;font-size:.8rem;margin-top:.35rem}.cb-controls{display:flex;gap:.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}.cb-controls button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.45rem .65rem;cursor:pointer}.cb-controls button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}.cb-controls span{margin-left:auto;font-size:.75rem}.cb-controls button:focus-visible,.cb-scene select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px}.cb-hold{height:3px;margin-top:.6rem;background:var(--color-rule)}.cb-hold span{display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--teal)}
@media(max-width:550px){.cb-scene{padding:.75rem}.cb-split{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cb-path{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.1rem}.cb-path li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}.cb-path li span{grid-row:1/3;grid-column:2}.cb-path li:not(:last-child)::after{content:'↓';right:50%;top:auto;bottom:-1.05rem}.cb-coverage span{font-size:.62rem}.cb-controls button{padding:.5rem .6rem}.cb-box dd{max-width:11rem}.cb-controls span{margin-left:0}}
</style>
